Re-verified at tip 601dee93cb: `install!`'s Usage block still rendered into the streaming root immediately and suggested polling for `__rf_payload`. It is replaced with a readiness-driven Reagent-slim recipe:
- its requires are named;
- the frame is made first;
- the container is bound before `install!`, because `:on-ready` may fire synchronously;
- `ssr/hydrate!` and then `reagent2.dom.client/hydrate-root` run only from `:on-ready`;
- there is no `create-root`, no early `hydrate-root` and no polling.

It is validated in the existing streaming DOM fixture, `re-frame.ssr.streaming-hydration-lifecycle-dom-cljs-test`, in the `cljs-browser` job:
- `the-install-recipe-boots-once-from-readiness-on-a-live-stream`: nothing seeds while the payload is in flight. Exactly one seed and hydration run after every wrapper is gone, with no React mismatch, and the server content is adopted.
- `the-install-recipe-boots-once-on-an-already-buffered-response`: the recipe boots synchronously inside `install!`, once.

