- the JVM lane is deps.edn's :test alias, re-frame.test-quiet.runner over test/;
- the same .cljc namespaces run in the CLJS node-test build configured by implementation/shadow-cljs.edn. CLJS counts go through the mayor's lane grant in ONE end window, or come from a CI run whose tree for this artefact is identical.

KEEP BY RULE:
- every test that IS the conformance contract for a spec-stated event-model property, meaning one that a spec section or an EP names, or that pins a public facade behaviour;
- tests of documented error ids (rf2-98kzs.3's ruling);
- regression pins.
A duplicate may go only when a kept test makes the same assertion on the same input and runs in every lane the removed one did. A conformance test that duplicates an assertion in core's OWN unit tests is not thereby redundant. The conformance tier exists to pin the contract from outside core, so such a test stays.

