description:
Mike, 2026-10-03 16:4x AUSEST, verbatim: "Can we add Fresco, HTTP and resourcs into the bundle." then "Create a PR".

The bundle is the docs playground's re-frame2 SCI engine (docs/tools/playground/sci/, built to docs/cljs/playground-rf2.js), which runs the site's cljs-rf2 live cells. Its README says today: "Fresco, routing, HTTP and resources are not in the bundle. A cell that requires one of them fails because the namespace is not found." Routing is NOT in this request: leave it out.

TASK. Make re-frame.fresco, re-frame.http and re-frame.resources (implementation/fresco, implementation/http, implementation/resources), with whatever public namespaces cells naturally require, available to cljs-rf2 cells, by following the README's own recipe "Adding an artefact to re-frame2 cells":
1. add each as a :local/root dep in sci/deps.edn;
2. require each in sci.cljs so its late-bind hooks install at load, add SCI namespaces for what cells require the way re-frame.schemas is added, and give each JVM-only macro an SCI stand-in;
3. add each source tree to the roster in scripts/playground-sci-input-digest.mjs and to the playground surface in .github/scripts/report-changed-surfaces.sh, with its mirror implementation/scripts/_changed-surfaces.test.cjs in the SAME commit; implementation/scripts/_playground-sci-inputs.test.cjs fails if a roster entry does not trigger the playground job;
4. add a smoke cell per artefact.
Then update the README's "What a re-frame2 cell can use" list, its "not in the bundle" sentence (routing only), the "four artefacts" count, and the sci/deps.edn header comment.

MODEL. PR #10482 added re-frame.schemas to this bundle in four commits (load, CI trigger, smoke cell, README). Follow its shape.

KNOWN SHAPE QUESTIONS for the worker to settle at source, not litigate: whether a Fresco view renders through the engine's renderLast as it stands or needs a branch there; how the HTTP smoke cell avoids the network (a stub transport or the artefact's own test seam, never a live fetch); whether resources pulls http in transitively; what bundle growth does to the tools-playground job's "plausible bundle" check.

